      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of unique pairings of teams:**\n   Each pair of teams plays exactly three games. Since there are 9 teams, the number of unique pairs of teams is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{9}{2} \\), which is the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9.\n   \\[\n   \\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n   \\]\n   So, there are 36 unique pairs of teams.\n\n2. **Determine the total number of games played:**\n   Each of these 36 unique pairs plays 3 games. Therefore, the total number of games played is:\n   \\[\n   36 \\times 3 = 108\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played in the season is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
