      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the number of teams and games played in each pair:**\n   Each team plays 3 games against each of the other 8 teams. Therefore, each team plays \\(3 \\times 8 = 24\\) games against the other teams.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of games:**\n   There are 9 teams, and each game involves 2 teams. So, the total number of games is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{9}{2} \\), which represents the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 to play a game. The formula for combinations is:\n   \\[\n   \\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n   \\]\n   This calculation confirms the total number of unique pairs of teams, and thus the total number of games played in the league.\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the league is \\(\\boxed{36}\\).",
