      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "### Problem:\nA baseball league consists of nine teams. Each team plays three games with every other team during the season. Determine the total number of games played in this season.\n\n1. **Determine the number of games each team plays:**\n   Each team plays 3 games against each of the 8 other teams.\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ games/team} \\times 8 \\text{ other teams} = 24 \\text{ games/team}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of games for all teams:**\n   There are 9 teams in total, and each team plays 24 games.\n   \\[\n   9 \\text{ teams} \\times 24 \\text{ games/team} = 216 \\text{ games}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Account for double counting:**\n   Each game involves two teams, so each game is counted twice in the sum of all individual game counts. To find the actual number of distinct games, we divide the total count by 2.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{216 \\text{ games}}{2} = 108 \\text{ distinct games}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   The total number of games played during the season is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{108}\n   \\]",
